        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NJp4nxZJ8VCDXqe9AtLvcz",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "1585\t**Verify:** `go test ./...` and `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...`\n1586\t\n1587\t**Why:** Every prior task tests one component against its own fixtures. This is the only task\n1588\tthat proves component N's output actually reaches component N+1 — particularly that the 2.0\n1589\tconversion path (Task 5) survives all the way to validation, and that the credential firewall\n1590\tholds across a whole session rather than one command at a time.\n1591\t\n1592\t---\n1593\t\n1594\t### Task 33: CI workflow running the test suite\n1595\t\n1596\t**Depends on:** Task 32\n1597\t\n1598\t**Test files:**\n1599\t- `internal/ci/workflow_test.go` (create) — the workflow file stays in step with `.ralph/stack.json`\n1600\t\n1601\t**Implementation files:**\n1602\t- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (create) — build, lint and test on push and pull request\n1603\t\n1604\t**Red — write failing tests:**\n1605\t1. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` parses as YAML and declares triggers for both `push` and\n1606\t   `pull_request`.\n1607\t2. Every shell command the workflow runs appears verbatim in `.ralph/stack.json`\n1608\t   (`build_command`, `lint_command`, `test_command`) — parse both files and compare, so the\n1609\t   workflow cannot drift into invented commands.\n1610\t3. The Go version pinned in the workflow matches the `go` directive in `go.mod`.\n1611\t4. The workflow runs `go test ./...`, which is what makes the Task 24 canary suite an actual\n1612\t   build gate rather than a test somebody has to remember to run.\n1613\t\n1614\t**Green — minimal implementation:**\n1615\t1. A single `ubuntu-latest` job: checkout, `actions/setup-go` pinned to the `go.mod` version,\n1616\t   then `go build ./...`, `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...`, `go test ./...`.\n1617\t2. Nothing else. **No release, matrix, cross-compilation or publishing step** — distribution is\n1618\t   out of scope (see Scope), and a release job here would quietly start Phase-9 work.\n1619\t3. curl is preinstalled on `ubuntu-latest` and is well above the 7.70 floor, so no install step\n1620\t   is needed; the Task 17 preflight covers the case where it is not.\n1621\t\n1622\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/ci/...` then `go build ./...` and\n1623\t`test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` and `go test ./...`\n1624\t\n1625\t**Why:** §5a requires that the canary suite \"gates every release thereafter\" and that \"redaction\n1626\tregressions fail the build\". Until a build exists, nothing gates anything — the suite is only a\n1627\tfile somebody could skip. This is the smallest thing that makes the design's own security\n1628\trequirement real, and the test keeps the workflow honest about which commands it runs.\n1629\t"
      }
    ]
  },
