        "type": "text",
        "text": "The conventions pass turned up nothing stale — every command in the CLI has a README section, and the JUnit output is documented correctly as `--report junit` (there is no `--junit` flag). No further doc commit needed.\n\n## Task 33 complete — CI workflow running the test suite\n\n**Red:** `internal/ci/workflow_test.go` — four tests, all failing because `.github/workflows/ci.yml` did not exist:\n- `TestWorkflowTriggersOnPushAndPullRequest` — parses the YAML, asserts both triggers\n- `TestWorkflowRunsOnlyStackCommands` — every `run:` in the workflow must appear verbatim in `.ralph/stack.json`, and all three of `build_command`/`lint_command`/`test_command` must actually run\n- `TestWorkflowRunsTheFullTestSuite` — `go test ./...` is among them, stated directly so the canary gate isn't just implied\n- `TestWorkflowPinsTheGoModVersion` — `actions/setup-go`'s `go-version` matches the `go` directive in `go.mod`\n\n**Green:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — one `ubuntu-latest` job: checkout, setup-go pinned to `1.26.0`, then `go build ./...`, `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...`, `go test ./...`. No release, matrix or cross-compilation step, per the plan's scope note. The lint command is a single-quoted YAML scalar so it stays byte-identical to the stack file.\n\n**Verification, all run and passing:**\n- `go test ./internal/ci/...` → ok\n- `go build ./...` → ok\n- `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` → ok\n- `go test ./...` → all 15 packages ok (canary 2.6s, e2e 1.9s ran fresh, not cached)\n\nTwo things worth noting. `.ralph/stack.json` is tracked in git — I checked before relying on it, since the test reads it at CI time and an untracked file would have failed on a fresh checkout. And I pinned `actions/checkout@v4` / `actions/setup-go@v5` rather than guessing at newer major tags.\n\nREADME's Building section now records that CI gates the leak suite. `tasks.json` task 33 is `done: true`, committed as `966a77e` along with the workflow, test and README.\n\nAll 33 tasks in `tasks.json` are now done. Stopping here — I have not archived the plan, reset `tasks.json`, or opened a PR, as those belong to later phases."
      }
