ctually covers every surface DESIGN.md §5a lists (json, pretty, tsv, dry-run, errors, junit, history store, corpus files, debug logs) — a surface it silently skips is a real finding.\n- **Injection**: argv construction via os/exec (never shell strings); the curl config document escaping (`data = \"...\"`, header values containing quotes/newlines/backslashes — can a crafted header or body value inject an arbitrary curl directive into the config document? e.g. a newline in a `--header` value adding `-o /etc/passwd` or `--upload-file`).\n- **Path traversal**: `--body @file`, `--fixtures dir/`, spec file paths, the local spec cache (internal/spec/source.go — is a URL-derived cache filename sanitized? can a crafted URL write outside the cache dir?), corpus paths.\n- **File permissions**: config file (design says mode 0600), history/corpus store files, temp files.\n- **SSRF / URL handling**: spec fetch by URL, `--base-url`.\n- **Secrets committed** in the diff (testdata, fixtures, CI workflow).\n- **CI workflow** (.github/workflows/ci.yml): unsafe use of untrusted PR input, overly broad permissions, script injection via `${{ }}` interpolation.\n\nVerify each candidate finding by actually reading the code and, where feasible, writing a tiny Go test or running the built binary (`go build ./... && ./talaria ...`) to confirm the failure. Do NOT report speculative issues you could not substantiate.\n\nReturn a list of findings. For each: title, severity (CRIT for exploitable leak/vuln or broken security functionality; WARN for missing hardening/validation; INFO for style), exact `path/to/file.go:LINE`, a description of what is wrong and why it matters, and a concrete suggested fix. If you confirmed it by running something, say what you ran and what you saw. Report nothing you did not verify.",
  "uuid": "5efb2280-4d93-4f21-a473-28d5cd9836fa",
