        "text": "You are the SPEC-COMPLIANCE reviewer for a code review of the git branch `ralph/design` in /home/casper/projects/talaria (Go CLI, cobra). Base branch is `main`. Review ONLY the branch diff: `git diff main...HEAD`. Do not report pre-existing issues outside the diff.\n\nSource of truth: `docs/design/DESIGN.md` (read it in full). Supporting: `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (the task breakdown), `tasks.json` (33 tasks, all marked done), `README.md`, `AGENT.md`, `docs/research/2026-08-02-design-review.md`.\n\n**Scope note:** this branch implements Phases 1–4 of DESIGN.md §7 (tasks 1–33). Phases 5–8 (recording proxy, `twin serve`, stateful twin, fault injection) are explicitly NOT in scope — do not report the twin as missing. `internal/twin/` being absent is correct.\n\nYour checklist:\n- **Completeness**: is every requirement in DESIGN.md §§3,4,5,5a for Phases 1–4 actually implemented? Walk the CLI surface in §4 command by command (`list`, `describe`, `search`, `uses`, `call` and every one of its flags, `history` / `history show` / `history replay` and its filters `--operation --since --status`, `run` with `--tag --operation --base-url --profile --allow-mutations --report json|junit|pretty --fail-on-error`, `auth check`, `version`) and verify each flag exists AND does what the doc says. Build the binary (`go build -o /tmp/talaria ./cmd/talaria`) and run `--help` on each command plus real invocations against the testdata specs to check.\n- **Correctness**: does behaviour match the doc's description, not just its name? Specifically verify: the exit-code table in §4 (0/1/2/3/4/5 semantics — especially that HTTP 4xx/5xx is exit 0 for `call` unless `--fail-on-error`, and exit 5 is credential-missing distinct from usage error 2); the `call` output envelope shape in §4 (\"Output shape for `call`\") including `schema: \"talaria/v1\"`, `request.curl`, `request.headers` with `<redacted:env:NAME>`, `response.timing_ms`, and the `validation` block fields `status_documented`/`body_valid`/`errors`; default output = pretty-on-TTY, JSON-when-piped with `--output` always winning; mutation gating (GET/HEAD/OPTIONS allowed, POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE require `--allow-mutations`); `--dry-run` sends nothing and exits 0; curl version floor >= 7.70 enforced (needs `--write-out '%{json}'`); the §3.2 compact schema format for `describe` (`name*: (string) description`, never raw JSON Schema); env var auth naming convention `TALARIA_AUTH_BEARER`, `TALARIA_AUTH_BASIC`, `TALARIA_AUTH_APIKEY_<SCHEME>`; `auth check` output shape `{\"scheme\":...,\"source\":\"env:...\",\"present\":true}`; the §5a \"Test data for `run` mode\" priority order (spec example/examples → `--fixtures` matched by operationId → `gen`); v1 auth scope bearer/basic/apikey in header, query AND cookie.\n- **Spec support**: Swagger 2.0 + OpenAPI 3.0/3.1/3.2, JSON and YAML, spec via positional arg / `--spec` / env var, file path or URL with local cache (§4 last lines, §5).\n- **Architecture boundary rules (§5 \"Key boundary rules\")**: verify with grep that `internal/operation`, `internal/validate`, `internal/gen` do NOT import `internal/curl` or `internal/twin`; that `secret` resolves values for exactly one caller (the curl executor). A violated boundary rule is a real finding.\n- **Non-goals (§9)**: anything implemented that §9 forbids (e.g. a `--show-secrets` flag, MCP server, interactive prompts/paging).\n- **Drift**: anything in the diff that contradicts the doc without a recorded reason. Note: the branch edits DESIGN.md itself (resolving the libopenapi-validator strictness open question) — check that edit is truthful against what `internal/validate` actually does and that the claimed fixture `internal/validate/testdata/strict-3.0.yaml` really exercises all four constructs named (nullable, boolean exclusiveMinimum/exclusiveMaximum, singular example).\n- **AGENT.md** (§3 principle 7, task 25): does it accurately document the actual flags, exit codes and output shapes? A doc that lies to an agent is a real bug.\n\nVerify by reading code AND running the binary. Do NOT report speculative issues.\n\nReturn a list of findings. For each: title, severity (CRIT for an unmet design-doc requirement / behaviour contradicting the doc / broken functionality; WARN for spec drift or partial implementation; INFO for doc gaps), exact `path/to/file.go:LINE`, description with the DESIGN.md section it violates, and a concrete suggested fix. Say what you ran and what you saw."
      }
    ]
  },
