        "content": "README.md:208:on top of the built-in `access_token`, `refresh_token` and `id_token`. `call` reads this file\nREADME.md:284:fields (`access_token`, `refresh_token`, `id_token`). A body in which nothing matched is\ninternal/secret/response.go:17:var builtinBodyPaths = []string{\"access_token\", \"refresh_token\", \"id_token\"}\ninternal/spec/source.go:48:// zero value is usable and caches under the user cache dir; tests set CacheDir\ninternal/spec/source.go:51:\t// CacheDir holds cached remote specs. Empty means\ninternal/spec/source.go:53:\tCacheDir string\ninternal/spec/source.go:63:\treturn (&Loader{}).Load(ref)\ninternal/spec/source.go:139:\tdir := l.CacheDir\ninternal/spec/source.go:141:\t\tbase, err := os.UserCacheDir()\ninternal/corpus/entry.go:191:// refresh_token, and a token-refresh request carries one in exactly that field.\nIMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:1265:  `refresh_token` and `id_token` in a response body are already redacted by default, so the\n---\nAGENT.md:184:JSON without asking. Every payload carries `\"schema\": \"talaria/v1\"` — branch on it if you cache\nREADME.md:49:specs are cached under `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/talaria/specs` (falling back to `~/.cache/talaria/specs`)\ndocs/design/DESIGN.md:220:Spec argument accepts a file path or URL (with local cache); falls back to an env var.\ndocs/design/DESIGN.md:253:internal/spec/             # load (file/URL/cache), v2→v3 convert, normalize\ndocs/design/DESIGN.md:343:| Spec cache, verbose/debug logs | Debug output goes through the same redacted representation. No `--verbose` that bypasses it |",
