        "text": "Review complete. `REVIEW_FINDINGS.md` committed as `b5afc96` — **20 findings: 11 CRIT, 7 WARN, 2 INFO**.\n\nBaseline first: `go build`, `gofmt`, `go vet`, and `go test -race ./...` all pass on the tracked tree. The bugs below are all in code the test suite exercises without catching.\n\n**The two that matter most, both in the credential firewall the product exists to be:**\n\n1. **Query-parameter credentials are never redacted** (`internal/request/build.go:76`) — `hide()` is applied to headers and cookies but not query. I reproduced it: `--header X-Api-Key=SECRET` renders `<redacted>`, the identically named `--query api_key=SECRET` renders verbatim in the emitted curl, the `url` field, and the on-disk `history.jsonl` — the artifact DESIGN.md §5a calls the highest-risk surface. The canary suite has no `--query` case, which is why it shipped.\n2. **Base-URL scheme is never validated** (`internal/request/build.go:141`) — the error message promises \"absolute http(s)\" but nothing checks. A spec whose own `servers[0].url` is `gopher://…` makes a plain `talaria call` deliver arbitrary bytes to an arbitrary TCP port, bypassing `--allow-mutations` entirely (that rail gates HTTP methods; gopher has none).\n\n**Other CRITs**, each verified by running the binary: HEAD operations emit `-X HEAD` instead of `--head` and hang forever (and there is *no* `max-time` anywhere, so a hung `run` emits no report at all — two separate findings); `corpus.trim` is an unlocked read-modify-write that silently dropped 57–61 of 80 concurrent appends in a probe test while returning `nil`; `run` sends generated JSON under the first-declared content type, so every converted Swagger 2.0 `formData` operation sends JSON labelled `x-www-form-urlencoded`; non-UTF-8 bodies are mangled to U+FFFD in the corpus and replayed at double length; the emitted curl uses `--data-binary` where the config document deliberately uses `data-raw`, so a `@`-leading body makes the \"paste this into a bug report\" command read a local file; unknown commands exit 1 (the retry code) instead of 2; `talaria version` ignores `--output`; and libopenapi logs to raw `os.Stdout`, putting two ERROR JSON documents on stdout for any spec with an unresolvable `$ref`.\n\nTwo judgement calls worth flagging: I kept **\"`run` alone never exits 4\"** at WARN — DESIGN.md §4's phrasing is genuinely ambiguous and README documents the implemented behaviour coherently, so it needs a decision, not an automatic fix. And the **`authorization` exact-match pattern** (misses `X-Authorization`, `Authentication`) is INFO because it implements §5a's list literally — the design is what's narrow, not the code."
      }
    ],
