ub/, .woodpecker.yml, Makefile all absent), so no CI-derived commands were available. No .claude/agents/ and no reviewer sections in the docs, so reviewer names are generic. Reviewer rationale: `security` is not routine here — the credential firewall (DESIGN.md §5a) IS the product, and DESIGN.md mandates a canary-secret CI suite in Phase 2 that greps every output surface (json/pretty/tsv/dry-run/errors/junit/history/corpus/debug logs) for injected secrets and fails the build on a leak. `concurrency` for the Phase 6+ twin HTTP server and recording proxy. `integration` for the CLI + twin server + proxy multi-process loop.\\n\\nRuntime deps: system curl is the execution engine and DESIGN.md sets a hard floor of curl >= 7.70 (needs --write-out '%{json}'). Installed here: curl 8.14.1 — satisfied. Go toolchain: go1.26.0 at /usr/local/go/bin/go. Module proxy is reachable (verified via `go list -m -versions github.com/spf13/cobra`), so dependency downloads work.\\n\\nNo database, no services, no .env required for Phases 1-4. Phase 7+ adds a bbolt store; consider adding a `performance` reviewer then. There are no pre-commit hooks. .gitignore already excludes /talaria, /dist/, /twin-data/, *.corpus/, .env* and config.local.yaml.\\n\\nPlanning inputs: docs/design/DESIGN.md is the source of truth (README.md says so explicitly) and contains an 8-phase roadmap in §7 with a deliberate decision gate after Phase 4. tasks.json at repo root points plan_file at IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, which does not exist yet.\"\n15\t}\n16\t"
