        "content": "1\t# talaria — Implementation Plan\n2\t\n3\tSource of truth: [docs/design/DESIGN.md](docs/design/DESIGN.md) (v0.3). Stack: `.ralph/stack.json`.\n4\t\n5\t## Scope\n6\t\n7\t**This plan covers Phases 1–4 only** (DESIGN.md §7). Phase 4 ends the differentiated core, and\n8\t§7 sets a deliberate decision gate there: *\"Do not start [5–8] on faith; start them because\n9\tusing Phases 1–4 made the absence of a twin painful.\"* Phases 5–8 (recording proxy, twin serve,\n10\tstateful twin, fault injection) are therefore **not planned here** and must not be started as\n11\tpart of this plan. When Task 33 passes, stop and hand the gate decision to a human.\n12\t\n13\tAlso deliberately **out of scope**, so no task should drift into them:\n14\t\n15\t- `internal/twin` and every `talaria twin …` subcommand (Phases 6–8).\n16\t- Distribution and packaging — cross-platform release binaries, `go install` docs, the install\n17\t  script, the Homebrew tap, the pi package and the Claude Code skill (DESIGN.md §7 lists these\n18\t  under distribution, not under a phase). Task 33 adds a CI workflow that runs the test suite;\n19\t  it deliberately does **not** build or publish releases.\n20\t- Request chaining / scenario DSL, OAuth flows, a built-in query language, and everything in §9\n21\t  Non-goals. `history replay` (Task 23) is the sanctioned substitute for chaining.\n22\t\n23\t## Commands (from `.ralph/stack.json` — do not invent others)\n24\t\n25\t| Purpose | Command |\n26\t|---|---|\n27\t| All tests | `go test ./...` |\n28\t| One package | `go test ./<dir>/...` (expansion of `test_single_command`) |\n29\t| Build | `go build ./...` |\n30\t| Lint | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` |\n31\t\n32\tRun lint before every commit. `golangci-lint` is **not** installed — do not add it to a task.\n33\t\n34\t## Ground facts (verified 2026-08-02, not assumed)\n35\t\n36\tModule path `github.com/Teeeep/talaria`; Go 1.26.0; curl 8.14.1 (design floor is ≥ 7.70).\n37\t\n38\tDependency versions, all resolvable from the module proxy:\n39\t\n40\t```\n41\tgithub.com/pb33f/libopenapi           v0.38.7\n42\tgithub.com/pb33f/libopenapi-validator v0.14.0\n43\tgithub.com/getkin/kin-openapi         v0.145.0\n44\tgithub.com/spf13/cobra                v1.10.2\n45\tgithub.com/spf13/viper                v1.21.0\n46\tgopkg.in/yaml.v3                      v3.0.1\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\t`yaml.v3` arrives transitively with libopenapi but Task 5 depends on it directly, so require it\n50\texplicitly rather than relying on a transitive edge.\n51\t\n52\t**libopenapi API** — `libopenapi.NewDocument(b []byte) (Document, error)`, then\n53\t`doc.BuildV3Model()` returning `(*DocumentModel[v3high.Document], error)` — a single `error`,\n54\t**not** a slice. Collections are `orderedmap` types iterated with `.FromOldest()`:\n55\t`m.Model.Paths.PathItems`, `pathItem.GetOperations()`, `op.Responses.Codes`,\n56\t`m.Model.Components.SecuritySchemes`, `m.Model.Components.Schemas`. A schema proxy yields the\n57\tschema via `.Schema()`; `schema.Type` is a `[]string`.\n58\t\n59\t**Swagger 2.0 bridge** — libopenapi cannot convert 2.0 (docs/research §1). The working path,\n60\trun end to end during planning: `json.Unmarshal(specBytes, &openapi2.T{})` →"
