        "text": "Planned. 11 CRIT findings → 9 fix tasks, committed as `fb90ced`.\n\n**Tasks (in order):**\n\n| # | Task | Findings |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Redact credentials passed in the query string | #1 |\n| 2 | Restrict base URLs and curl to http/https | #2 |\n| 3 | Correct curl for HEAD + rendered body flag matches wire | #3, #8 |\n| 4 | Bound the curl subprocess with timeouts | #4 |\n| 5 | Serialise history appends with a file lock | #5 |\n| 6 | Send `run`'s generated body under its real media type | #6 |\n| 7 | Preserve non-UTF-8 bodies in the corpus, refuse lossy replays | #7 |\n| 8 | CLI contract: usage exit 2, `version` JSON envelope | #9, #10 |\n| 9 | Stop libopenapi logging to stdout | #11 |\n\n**Two groupings:** #3 and #8 are both `internal/curl` emitting the wrong curl option (`-X HEAD`, `--data-binary`) and land in the same two files. #9 and #10 are both small `cmd/talaria` contract breaks against DESIGN.md §3.1/§4. The 7 WARN and 2 INFO findings produced no tasks.\n\n**One suggested fix I changed rather than copied.** Finding 1 says `Request.QueryString` should branch on `IsSensitive()` instead of `IsSecret()`. That would be a wire bug: `QueryString` is shared with the resolving path (`req.URL(resolve)` at `internal/curl/config.go:71`), so skipping `url.QueryEscape` there would put an unescaped credential in the real request URL. Task 1 instead instructs skipping the escape only when the rendered text is a placeholder (`value == p.Value.String() || value == p.Value.Symbolic()`), mirroring the comparison `word.credential` already makes at `internal/curl/render.go:201`. The `urlWord` half of that finding is display-only and is applied as suggested.\n\nTask 8's step 1 relies on `cobra.NoArgs` producing the `unknown command %q for %q` message and root staying non-runnable so bare `talaria` still prints help — worth the build phase confirming both in the same test run."
      }
    ],
