        "type": "text",
        "text": "Task 1 complete and committed.\n\n**What was wrong:** `--query` values never went through `hide()`, so a credential-shaped query name (`api_key`, `*token*`, `*secret*`) was printed verbatim on every output surface. The canary suite reproduced it — 4–5 leaking surfaces per output format, including `history.jsonl`.\n\n**The fix** (three places, per the plan):\n- `internal/request/build.go:76` — `req.Query` now wrapped in `hide()`, like headers and cookies.\n- `internal/curl/render.go` — `urlWord` branches on `IsSensitive()` rather than `IsSecret()`, so a hidden literal renders `<redacted>` instead of `%3Credacted%3E`. Safe because that path is display-only.\n- `internal/request/request.go` — `QueryString` skips the percent-encode **only** when the rendered text is a placeholder (`value == p.Value.String() || value == p.Value.Symbolic()`), not whenever the value is sensitive. This function is shared with the wire path, so a resolved credential must still be escaped.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `go test ./...` — all 15 packages green; `go build ./...` and `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` clean.\n- Red confirmed first: the three new/extended tests failed for the right reason (canary leaked across pretty/json/tsv, render emitted `%3Credacted%3E`).\n- All three plan checkboxes checked against a real binary and a local server: dry-run shows `<redacted>` in both `curl` and `url`; `history.jsonl` holds only the placeholder; the wire form still arrived correctly encoded — `PATH: /public?api_key=a+b%26c` for the value `a b&c`.\n\nStopping here — 8 tasks remain in `tasks.json` for the next iteration."
      }
    ],
