          "command": "git add -A internal cmd README.md tasks.json && git status --short && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix: restrict base URLs and curl to http and https\n\nA base URL is untrusted input from every direction: --base-url, a profile, and\na spec's servers[0].url, which the product's premise says an agent may have\nfound anywhere. Only the host and a non-empty scheme were checked, so\n`gopher://127.0.0.1:1234` built cleanly and curl — which speaks file, gopher,\ndict and smb — would have made a raw TCP write or a local file read out of\n\"call this operation\".\n\n- request.IsHTTPScheme is the one rule, applied case-insensitively per RFC 3986\n  so HTTPS:// still works.\n- binder.baseURL now matches the error it already printed (\"is not an absolute\n  http(s) URL\") for all three candidate sources.\n- The curl config document carries proto = \"=http,https\" and\n  proto-redir = \"=http,https\", so a scheme that slips past the check, or a\n  redirect choosing its own next hop, still cannot leave http(s). Verified\n  against curl 8.14.1: `file://` is refused with exit 1.\n- replayRequest re-checks the scheme of the URL it rebuilds, because the store\n  is a file on disk and an edited entry must not replay as a file read.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1",
