        "content": "123\t### Task 3: Emit correct curl for HEAD, and make the rendered body flag match the wire\n124\t\n125\t**Fixes findings:** #3, #8\n126\t\n127\t**Files:**\n128\t- `internal/curl/config.go` (modify)\n129\t- `internal/curl/render.go` (modify)\n130\t- `internal/curl/config_test.go` (modify)\n131\t- `internal/curl/render_test.go` (modify)\n132\t\n133\t**Steps:**\n134\t1. In `document.build` (config.go:77), when `req.Method == \"HEAD\"` emit the bare `head` flag\n135\t   instead of `request = \"HEAD\"`. `-X HEAD` makes curl wait for a `Content-Length` body a\n136\t   compliant server never sends, so the call hangs (or exits 18 against HTTP/1.0), and because\n137\t   `HEAD` is in `safeMethods` a single HEAD operation makes `talaria run` never terminate.\n138\t2. With `head`, curl writes the header block to the output file, which would land in the response\n139\t   *body*. For `HEAD`, point the `output` directive at `os.DevNull` instead of\n140\t   `capture.BodyPath`; `dump-header` still captures the headers, and the staged (empty) body file\n141\t   keeps `readResponse` unchanged.\n142\t3. In `Render` (render.go:35), render `HEAD` as `-I` rather than `-X HEAD`, so the emitted\n143\t   command reproduces the call instead of hanging when pasted.\n144\t4. In `bodyArgs` (render.go:115), use `--data-raw` instead of `--data-binary`, matching the\n145\t   `data-raw` the config document deliberately uses (config.go:169 carries the reason: `data` and\n146\t   `data-binary` read a leading `@` as a filename, and a body legitimately can start with one).\n147\t   Without this, a `--body @file` whose contents start with `@` sends the literal text on the\n148\t   wire while the emitted command reads a local file and exfiltrates it.\n149\t5. Tests: a HEAD operation builds a config with `head` and no `request = \"HEAD\"`, renders `-I`,\n150\t   and — as an executor test against a local server answering HEAD with `Content-Length` and no\n151\t   body — completes rather than hanging. A render test with a body of `@/etc/hostname` pins\n152\t   `--data-raw` and pins the two paths together.\n153\t\n154\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/curl/...`\n155\t- [ ] `talaria call headspec.yaml headThing` against a server that answers HEAD returns promptly\n156\t      with a status instead of exiting 124/18.\n157\t- [ ] The emitted command for a body starting with `@` sends that text as data when pasted.\n158\t\n159\t---\n160\t"
      }
    ]
  },
