        "content": "1\t# talaria — Review Fix Plan\n2\t\n3\tSource of truth: [docs/design/DESIGN.md](docs/design/DESIGN.md) (v0.3). Stack: `.ralph/stack.json`.\n4\tFindings: [REVIEW_FINDINGS.md](REVIEW_FINDINGS.md) — do not edit that file.\n5\t\n6\t## Scope\n7\t\n8\tThis plan replaces the Phase 1–4 build plan, which is complete (tasks 1–33 all `done`). It\n9\tcovers **only the 11 CRIT findings** from the review of `ralph/design` vs `main`. The 7 WARN and\n10\t2 INFO findings are deliberately **not** planned: they are recorded for a human and do not block\n11\tthe PR. Do not create work for them, and do not \"fix them while you are in the file\" — an\n12\tunrequested change in a reviewed diff costs another review cycle.\n13\t\n14\tStill out of scope, unchanged from the build plan: Phases 5–8 (`internal/twin`, the recording\n15\tproxy, `talaria twin …`), distribution and packaging, request chaining, and everything in\n16\tDESIGN.md §9 Non-goals.\n17\t\n18\t## Commands (from `.ralph/stack.json` — do not invent others)\n19\t\n20\t| Purpose | Command |\n21\t|---|---|\n22\t| All tests | `go test ./...` |\n23\t| One package | `go test ./<dir>/...` (expansion of `test_single_command`) |\n24\t| Build | `go build ./...` |\n25\t| Lint | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` |\n26\t\n27\tRun the build and lint before every commit. `golangci-lint` is **not** installed. The tracked\n28\ttree passes `go build ./...`, `gofmt -l .`, `go vet ./...` and `go test -race ./...` today, so\n29\tany failure after a task is that task's doing.\n30\t\n31\t## Rules for these tasks\n32\t\n33\t- Every task adds or extends a test that **fails before the fix and passes after**. A CRIT\n34\t  finding that ships with no regression test comes back.\n35\t- Redaction changes go through the canary suite (`internal/canary`), which DESIGN.md §5a calls\n36\t  the release gate — extend it rather than only asserting in a unit test.\n37\t- Keep the existing comment style: these files explain *why*, not *what*. A fix that lands with\n38\t  no explanation of the invariant it restores is half the change.\n39\t\n40\t## Task order\n41\t\n42\tTasks 1–2 are the credential-firewall breaches (§5a) and come first. Tasks 3–4 are the curl\n43\texecution contract. Tasks 5–7 are data integrity. Tasks 8–9 are the CLI/output contract. There\n44\tare no dependencies between tasks; the order is by severity of consequence.\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t"
