        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Ug6pM783SH9WbdPePuxSPE",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "161\t### Task 4: Bound the curl subprocess with connect and total timeouts\n162\t\n163\t**Fixes findings:** #4\n164\t\n165\t**Files:**\n166\t- `internal/curl/config.go` (modify)\n167\t- `internal/curl/exec.go` (modify)\n168\t- `cmd/talaria/call.go` (modify)\n169\t- `cmd/talaria/run.go` (modify)\n170\t- `internal/curl/exec_test.go` (modify)\n171\t\n172\t**Steps:**\n173\t1. Add an exported options type to `internal/curl` carrying `ConnectTimeout` and `MaxTime`\n174\t   (`time.Duration`), with defaults (10s connect, 30s total). Thread it through `BuildConfig` and\n175\t   `Execute` by adding an `ExecuteWith(req, opts)` / `BuildConfigWith(req, capture, opts)` pair\n176\t   and keeping `Execute(req)` / `BuildConfig(req, capture)` as the default-options wrappers, so\n177\t   existing call sites and tests keep compiling.\n178\t2. In `document.build`, emit `connect-timeout` and `max-time` directives from those options.\n179\t   curl enforces them itself and exits 28, which `runFailure` already classifies as a request\n180\t   failure (exit 1), so the happy path needs no Go-side plumbing.\n181\t3. In `Execute`, use `exec.CommandContext` with a context whose deadline is `MaxTime` plus a\n182\t   small margin, and set `cmd.WaitDelay`, so a curl that ignores its own timeout is still killed\n183\t   and reaped rather than leaving talaria blocked forever.\n184\t4. Add a `--timeout` flag (seconds, total) to `call` and `run`, defaulting to the package\n185\t   default, and pass it through. `run` is the reason this is CRIT: without a bound, the suite\n186\t   stalls on operation *k* of *n* and emits no report at all, so an agent or CI gets nothing.\n187\t5. Test against a local server that accepts the connection and never responds: `ExecuteWith` with\n188\t   a short `MaxTime` returns a request-failure error within the timeout instead of blocking, and\n189\t   the built document contains both directives.\n190\t\n191\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/curl/... ./cmd/talaria/...`\n192\t- [ ] A call against a never-answering server fails with exit 1 inside the timeout.\n193\t- [ ] `talaria run` over a spec containing such an operation still emits its report.\n194\t"
      }
    ]
  },
