          "command": "git add -A internal/curl cmd/talaria README.md AGENT.md docs/design/DESIGN.md tasks.json && git status --short && git commit -q -m \"fix: bound the curl subprocess with connect and total timeouts\n\ncurl ran with no connect-timeout and no max-time, and exec.Command gave the\nsubprocess no deadline of its own, so an API that accepted a connection and\nnever answered blocked talaria indefinitely. Worst for run: the suite stalled on\noperation k of n and emitted no report at all.\n\ncurl.Options carries the two bounds (10s connect, 30s total by default) through\nBuildConfigWith and ExecuteWith, with the old signatures kept as default-options\nwrappers. The document emits connect-timeout and max-time, which curl enforces\nitself and reports as exit 28 — already classified as a failed request.\nexec.CommandContext plus WaitDelay at max-time + 2s is the backstop for a curl\nthat ignores them. call and run take --timeout in seconds; on run it bounds each\noperation, so one wedged endpoint costs a line rather than the report.\" && git log --oneline -1",
