        "type": "text",
        "text": "Task 4 complete and committed (`828ade8`). Stopping here.\n\n**What was built** — Finding #4 (CRIT): the curl subprocess had no timeout of any kind.\n\n- `internal/curl/config.go`: new `Options{ConnectTimeout, MaxTime}` with defaults 10s/30s, `BuildConfigWith(req, capture, opts)`; `BuildConfig` is now the default-options wrapper. `document.build` emits `connect-timeout` and `max-time` directives — curl enforces them and exits 28, which `runFailure` already classifies as a failed request (exit 1). Non-positive values fall back to the default rather than meaning \"unbounded\"; a connect timeout above the total is clamped.\n- `internal/curl/exec.go`: `ExecuteWith(req, opts)` uses `exec.CommandContext` with a deadline of `MaxTime + 2s` and sets `cmd.WaitDelay`, so a curl that ignores its own timeout is killed and reaped; that path reports a distinct message instead of a bogus exit status.\n- `cmd/talaria/call.go`, `run.go`: `--timeout` (seconds, default 30) threaded through; on `run` it bounds each operation via a new `runner.opts`.\n\n**Tests (red first, then green)**\n- `TestBuildConfigBoundsTheCallInTime` / `TestBuildConfigWithUsesTheGivenTimeouts` — directives present, sub-second values rendered as decimals.\n- `TestExecuteWithGivesUpOnAServerThatNeverAnswers` — raw listener that accepts and never replies; returns a `CodeRequestFailed` error with `curl exited 28` well inside the bound.\n- `TestRunStillReportsWhenAnOperationTimesOut` — `run --timeout 1` against that listener still emits its JSON report with the operation failed. Both new tests failed for the right reasons first (undefined `Options`/`ExecuteWith`; `unknown flag: --timeout`).\n\n**Verification**: `go build ./...` clean, `go test ./...` all packages ok, `go test -race ./internal/curl/... ./cmd/talaria/...` ok, `gofmt`/`go vet` clean. No `--no-verify` used.\n\n**Docs**: `--timeout` added to the `call` and `run` surfaces in DESIGN.md §4, plus the timeout behaviour in README.md and AGENT.md (per-operation on `run`)."
      }
    ],
