    "content": [
      {
        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01BU9aZuJCnAHmMoJxye371J",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "360\tenvironment exactly as the original call did — history holds their *names*, so there is nothing\n361\tin the file to read back. It is gated the same way `call` is: replaying a `POST` needs\n362\t`--allow-mutations`. A header whose value was a literal talaria redacted by name cannot be\n363\treproduced, and replay says so on stderr rather than pretending it sent one.\n364\t\n365\tEntries are written **redacted, at write time**. The store is the highest-risk artifact talaria\n366\tproduces, so un-redacted recording is not an option and there is no flag for it. It lives at\n367\t`$XDG_STATE_HOME/talaria/history.jsonl` (falling back to `~/.local/state/talaria/`), directory\n368\t`0700` and file `0600`, one JSON entry per line, keeping the most recent 1000 entries *per\n369\tsource* and truncating bodies at 64 KiB with an explicit `\"truncated\": true`.\n370\t\n371\tRecording is off for a profile that says so, and off everywhere when the environment says so:\n372\t\n373\t```yaml\n374\tprofiles:\n375\t  prod:\n376\t    history:\n377\t      enabled: false"
      }
    ]
  },
  "parent_tool_use_id": null,
  "session_id": "3d6a7496-a0d0-44bf-a370-5b836be66f57",
