        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "225\t- [ ] The concurrency test loses zero entries where the pre-fix code lost ~60 of 80.\n226\t- [ ] Two `talaria` processes appending to the same `history.jsonl` both keep their entries.\n227\t\n228\t---\n229\t\n230\t### Task 6: Send `run`'s generated body under the media type it was generated from\n231\t\n232\t**Fixes findings:** #6\n233\t\n234\t**Files:**\n235\t- `internal/gen/fixtures.go` (modify)\n236\t- `cmd/talaria/run.go` (modify)\n237\t- `internal/gen/fixtures_test.go` (modify)\n238\t- `cmd/talaria/run_test.go` (modify)\n239\t\n240\t**Steps:**\n241\t1. `bodySchema` (fixtures.go:223) deliberately picks the *JSON* media type to generate from, but\n242\t   that choice is never communicated onward: `run` passes only the bytes and\n243\t   `binder.contentType` (request/body.go:123) independently picks `rb.Content[0].ContentType`.\n244\t   When JSON is not first they disagree — and on the Swagger 2.0 path every converted `formData`\n245\t   operation sends a JSON body under `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`.\n246\t2. Have `bodySchema` return the media type alongside the schema, and add a `ContentType` field to\n247\t   `gen.Data` recording the media type the body was actually generated for. When the body came\n248\t   from a fixture and the operation declares no content, use `application/json` — `compact`\n249\t   already treats a fixture body as JSON.\n250\t3. In `runner.execute` (run.go:329), when `data.Body` is non-nil and `data.ContentType` is\n251\t   non-empty, add `Content-Type: <media type>` to the headers passed as `request.Inputs.Headers`\n252\t   — unless a fixture header already set one. `binder.contentType` already lets a user-set header\n253\t   win, so nothing else changes.\n254\t4. Tests: a 3.0 spec declaring `application/xml` before `application/json` produces a request\n255\t   with `Content-Type: application/json`; a converted Swagger 2.0 `formData` operation likewise;\n256\t   a fixture-supplied `Content-Type` still wins.\n257\t\n258\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/gen/... ./cmd/talaria/...`\n259\t- [ ] The request `run` builds carries a `Content-Type` matching the bytes in its body.\n260\t- [ ] A smoke run against a strict server no longer reports a spec bug that is talaria's.\n261\t\n262\t---\n263\t\n264\t### Task 7: Preserve non-UTF-8 request bodies in the corpus, and refuse lossy replays"
      }
    ]
  },
