{
  "type": "user",
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
      {
        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MXYw9A67zjQGufY7PdERs7",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "curl, and returns the request and the response as one structured block. `--param` takes a\nparameter the operation declares, in any location; `--query` and `--header` add ones it does\nnot, and all three repeat. Every binding problem is reported at once, so a wrong parameter name\nand a missing required one arrive in the same message rather than one run apart.\n\n`--body` supplies a request body three ways: a literal (`--body '{\"name\":\"Rex\"}'`), a file\n(`--body @pet.json`, read verbatim), or `--body -` to read talaria's own stdin. The bytes are\nresolved in the Go process before curl exists, so a body on stdin and the credentials curl\nreads on *its* stdin never share a pipe. The content type is the `Content-Type` you set with\n`--header`, otherwise the media type the operation declares.\n\nThe emitted command references credentials by environment-variable name and never by value:\n\n```\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TALARIA_AUTH_BEARER\" 'https://api.example.com/v1/pets/42?verbose=true'\n```",
        "is_error": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "parent_tool_use_id": null,
  "session_id": "4612972a-09f0-4988-bf02-53853a0500aa",
