        "text": "Task 7 done and committed. Stopping here per one-task-per-session.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `internal/corpus/entry.go` — added `Body.Encoding` (`EncodingBase64 = \"base64\"`) and `Body.Bytes()`. `newBody` now checks `utf8.Valid` after truncation: valid UTF-8 is stored verbatim exactly as before, anything else is base64'd. `Bytes()` refuses an unrecognised encoding with a `clierr.Usage` error rather than reading it as literal text.\n- `cmd/talaria/history.go` — `replayRequest` decodes via `body.Bytes()` instead of `[]byte(body.Data)`; new `bodyLine` helper so `history show` prints `<binary body, 1024 bytes, base64 in --output json>` rather than a base64 blob passed off as the body.\n- Tests: new `internal/corpus/entry_test.go` (round-trip of all 256 byte values ×4, UTF-8 stored verbatim, unknown encoding refused, undecodable base64 refused) and three tests in `cmd/talaria/history_test.go` (replay sends the original bytes, replay refuses an unknown encoding, show doesn't print binary as text).\n- `README.md` — documented the `encoding` field in the history store description.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- Red confirmed for the right reason before the fix: `the replay carries 1368 bytes, want the recorded 1024` and `the round trip returned 2048 bytes, want the original 1024`.\n- `go test ./...` — all 15 packages ok.\n- `go build ./...` and `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` — clean.\n\nRemaining: tasks 8 (CLI contract) and 9 (libopenapi stdout logs)."
