        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01AyE9CtduyUjBqFAaDLLhx6",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "296\t---\n297\t\n298\t### Task 8: Restore the CLI contract — usage exit code for unknown commands, JSON envelope for `version`\n299\t\n300\t**Fixes findings:** #9, #10\n301\t\n302\t**Files:**\n303\t- `cmd/talaria/root.go` (modify)\n304\t- `cmd/talaria/version.go` (modify)\n305\t- `cmd/talaria/exitcode_test.go` (modify)\n306\t- `cmd/talaria/version_test.go` (modify)\n307\t\n308\t**Steps:**\n309\t1. `talaria bogus` exits 1, because cobra's \"unknown command\" error is never classified and\n310\t   `exitCode` treats an unclassified error as a request failure. DESIGN.md §4 assigns 2 to usage\n311\t   errors, and exit 1 is the code AGENT.md tells an agent is transient and worth retrying — so a\n312\t   typo sends the agent into a retry loop. Fix by setting `Args: usageArgs(cobra.NoArgs)` on the\n313\t   root command: `cobra.NoArgs` produces exactly the `unknown command %q for %q` message, and\n314\t   `usageArgs` already wraps it as `clierr.Usage`. Bare `talaria` still prints help and exits 0,\n315\t   because `ValidateArgs` passes on an empty argument list and cobra then returns `flag.ErrHelp`.\n316\t2. `version` (version.go:17) `fmt.Fprintf`s `talaria dev` unconditionally, ignoring `--output`.\n317\t   DESIGN.md §3.1 and AGENT.md:183 both promise `--output json` on *every* command with the\n318\t   `talaria/v1` envelope — and this is the one command an agent uses to check compatibility.\n319\t   Route it through `resolveFormat(cmd)` + `output.New(format, cmd.OutOrStdout()).Render(...)`\n320\t   with a payload of `{\"version\": version}`, exactly as `list` does. Keep the bare\n321\t   `talaria <version>` string as the pretty rendering, and give the payload a `Table` so `tsv`\n322\t   renders too.\n323\t3. Tests: `talaria bogus` exits 2 and its stderr envelope carries `\"code\":2`; `talaria version\n324\t   --output json` emits one object with `\"schema\":\"talaria/v1\"` and a `version` field;\n325\t   `--output pretty` is unchanged from today.\n326\t\n327\t**Verify:** `go test ./cmd/talaria/...`\n328\t- [ ] `talaria bogus` → exit 2. `talaria` with no arguments → help, exit 0.\n329\t- [ ] Every command's stdout under `--output json` parses as the versioned envelope.\n330\t\n331\t---"
      }
    ]
  },
