        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01AVjqMS1pR9rDjyZa75GRQY",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "134:Exit codes follow `call`: failures exit 0 unless you pass `--fail-on-error`, which makes them\n135-exit 4. A missing credential exits **5** whichever flags you passed — that operation was never\n136-tested, so ask a human to export the variable named in its `reason`. Every request `run` makes is\n137-recorded in history with `\"source\": \"run\"`, and `history --source call` filters them back out.\n138-\n139-## Credentials\n140-\n141-You cannot read a credential and you do not need to. talaria maps each security scheme the spec\n142-declares onto an environment variable, and carries the name:\n143-\n144-| Scheme in the spec | Variable |\n145-|---|---|\n146-| `type: http`, `scheme: bearer` | `TALARIA_AUTH_BEARER` |\n147-| `type: http`, `scheme: basic` | `TALARIA_AUTH_BASIC` (`user:password`) |\n148-| `type: apiKey`, named `petKey` | `TALARIA_AUTH_APIKEY_PETKEY` (scheme name, upper-cased) |\n149-\n150-```sh\n151-talaria auth check ./openapi.yaml\n152-{\"scheme\":\"bearerAuth\",\"source\":\"env:TALARIA_AUTH_BEARER\",\"present\":true}\n153-```\n154-\n--\n201:## Exit codes\n202-\n203-| Code | Meaning | What to do |\n204-|---|---|---|\n205-| 0 | Success. A 4xx/5xx response is still success | read `response.status` |\n206-| 1 | The request could not be completed: network, TLS, curl itself | check the host and `--base-url`; retrying once is reasonable |\n207-| 2 | Usage error: unknown operation, missing parameter, bad flag, or a mutation without `--allow-mutations` | fix the invocation using `valid_alternatives` and the message |\n208-| 3 | The spec could not be read or parsed | check the path or URL; do not retry unchanged |\n209-| 4 | With `--fail-on-error`: the response was an HTTP error or violated the spec | read the `validation` block and `response.status` on stdout; report what failed |\n210-| 5 | A required credential is not set | tell a human which variable to export; do not retry until they have |\n211-\n212-## History\n213-\n214-Every real call is recorded, redacted at write time, newest first. Use it instead of re-issuing a\n215-request to remember what happened:\n216-\n217-```sh\n218-talaria history --operation getPet --status 4xx\n219-talaria history show 3\n220-```\n221-",
        "is_error": false
      }
    ]
  },
