        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "commit f7475864ecc9033a3f51cb75e74ed9acce3da5cb\nAuthor: Teeeep <casperjantepe@gmail.com>\nDate:   Sun Aug 2 20:59:00 2026 +0000\n\n    fix: exit 2 on an unknown command and render version through the envelope\n    \n    An unknown command reached exitCode as cobra's bare Find error and exited 1 —\n    the code AGENT.md calls transient and worth retrying, so a typo could send an\n    agent into a retry loop. The root command now rejects positional arguments\n    itself as a clierr.Usage error (exit 2), carrying near misses as\n    valid_alternatives; it gains a RunE because cobra only validates args on a\n    runnable command, and that RunE prints the help bare `talaria` used to get for\n    free.\n    \n    `version` ignored --output and printed a bare line, though DESIGN.md §3.1 and\n    AGENT.md promise the talaria/v1 envelope on every command — and it is the one\n    command an agent calls to check compatibility. It now renders through\n    output.New: {\"schema\":\"talaria/v1\",\"version\":\"dev\"} for json, the unchanged\n    `talaria dev` line for pretty and tsv.\n\n211:## Finding 11: libopenapi writes structured error logs directly to `os.Stdout`, corrupting the envelope\n215:- **Description:** `libopenapi.NewDocument(data)` leaves `d.config == nil`, so `BuildV3Model` falls\n217:  `slog.New(slog.NewJSONHandler(os.Stdout, …))` (libopenapi@v0.38.7/datamodel/document_config.go:233).\n224:- **Suggested fix:** Use `libopenapi.NewDocumentWithConfiguration` with a configuration whose `Logger`",
