        "type": "tool_use",
        "id": "toolu_01MCbdfgJ25qWksg8UNjJmDX",
        "name": "Bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "git add internal/spec tasks.json && git status --short && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -1\nfix: keep libopenapi's diagnostics off stdout\n\n`libopenapi.NewDocument(data)` left the document config nil, so BuildV3Model\nfell back to a default whose logger is a JSON slog handler writing to the real\nos.Stdout — past cmd.OutOrStdout, past the talaria/v1 envelope and past every\nredaction path. A spec with an unresolvable $ref put two\n{\"time\":…,\"level\":\"ERROR\"} documents on stdout and nothing else, so an agent\nparsing that stream got log lines where the envelope belongs.\n\nParsing now goes through NewDocumentWithConfiguration with the logger pointed at\nio.Discard; stdout belongs to the envelope, and the error still comes back as a\nclierr.SpecLoad (exit 3) rendered through it on stderr. AllowFileReferences and\nAllowRemoteReferences stay at their false defaults — naming the configuration\nexplicitly is exactly where that protection could be dropped, so both are now\npinned by tests alongside one that swaps os.Stdout for a pipe and asserts the\nfile descriptor stays silent.\nEOF",
          "description": "Commit the fix"
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      }
    ],
