        "content": "90\t### Task 2: Restrict base URLs and curl to http and https\n91\t\n92\t**Fixes findings:** #2\n93\t\n94\t**Files:**\n95\t- `internal/request/build.go` (modify)\n96\t- `internal/curl/config.go` (modify)\n97\t- `cmd/talaria/history.go` (modify)\n98\t- `internal/request/build_test.go` (modify)\n99\t- `internal/curl/config_test.go` (modify)\n100\t\n101\t**Steps:**\n102\t1. In `binder.baseURL` (build.go:141), reject any scheme other than `http` and `https`, making\n103\t   the check match the error message it already prints (\"is not an absolute http(s) URL\").\n104\t   Compare case-insensitively. This applies to all three candidate sources — `--base-url`, the\n105\t   profile, and `firstServer(b.in.Doc)` — because a spec's `servers[0].url` is untrusted input:\n106\t   the product's premise is that an agent points talaria at any doc it found.\n107\t2. In `document.build` (config.go), emit `proto = \"=http,https\"` and `proto-redir = \"=http,https\"`\n108\t   as defence in depth, so a scheme that slips past step 1 or arrives via a redirect still cannot\n109\t   make curl speak gopher, file, dict or smb.\n110\t3. In `replayRequest` (history.go:494), apply the same scheme check to the URL rebuilt from the\n111\t   stored entry, returning `clierr.Usage` naming the offending scheme.\n112\t4. Test: a spec whose `servers[0].url` is `gopher://127.0.0.1:1234` fails to build with a usage\n113\t   error; `--base-url file:///etc/passwd` likewise; `http` and `https` still build. Assert the\n114\t   two `proto` directives are present in the built config document.\n115\t\n116\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/request/... ./internal/curl/... ./cmd/talaria/...`\n117\t- [ ] `talaria call spec.yaml getPub --base-url gopher://127.0.0.1:18201 --dry-run` exits 2 with\n118\t      a usage error instead of emitting a gopher command.\n119\t- [ ] A spec declaring a `gopher://` server cannot deliver a payload to a raw TCP listener.\n120\t"
      }
