    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Committed as `b0c7c90`. Nine fix tasks from the nine CRIT findings; the 16 WARN and 10 INFO findings produced no tasks.\n\n**Tasks 1–5 — credential firewall (§5a), the bulk of the CRIT set:**\n1. `curl -q` so a writable `~/.curlrc` can't `trace-ascii` the resolved token out of the `-K` document\n2. Stop echoing a rejected `--header`/`--body` value into the exit-2 JSON\n3. Reject userinfo in a base URL (`--base-url`, profile, **and the spec's `servers[0].url`**) before it reaches `history.jsonl`\n4. Thread `redact.headers` into `hide()` — today it protects the store but not stdout, exactly inverted\n5. Make response-body redaction descend into arrays, and retarget the unit test that currently asserts the leak as correct\n\n**6–9:** signal handling so a killed talaria doesn't orphan curl or leave the raw capture on disk; stable ids on history entries so `replay <n>` stops re-issuing the wrong request; `talaria auth <typo>` → exit 2; and the `--header 'Name: value'` doc lines corrected with an `agentdoc_test.go` that actually executes AGENT.md's invocations.\n\nTwo judgment calls worth flagging:\n\n- **Findings 2 and 9 overlap in `binder.pairs`.** Finding 9's silent-corruption half (`--header 'X-Trace: abc=1'` is accepted and sends the malformed `X-Trace: abc: 1`) is a code fix in the same function as finding 2's message leak, so I merged it into Task 2 and left Task 9 as docs plus the test gate. Same file, same function, same kind of fix — splitting them would have meant two tasks editing one function.\n- **Finding 9 suggests also accepting the curl-style `Name: value` form.** I deliberately didn't plan that: DESIGN.md §4 specifies `name=value` and the code implements it, so widening the CLI contract is a design change, not a review fix. Task 2 rejects the colon form cleanly and Task 9 corrects the docs to match. If you'd rather accept both forms, that's a design-doc amendment first.\n\nOne thing the plan asks for that's worth watching in the build phase: Task 6 needs a `syscall.SysProcAttr` build-tag split to keep the non-unix build compiling, which is the largest change in the set."
      }
    ],
