        "content": "40\t  the release gate — extend it rather than only asserting in a unit test.\n41\t- Keep the existing comment style: these files explain *why*, not *what*. A fix that lands with\n42\t  no explanation of the invariant it restores is half the change.\n43\t\n44\t## Task order\n45\t\n46\tTasks 1–5 are the credential-firewall breaches (§5a) and come first. Task 6 is the curl execution\n47\tcontract. Task 7 is data integrity. Tasks 8–9 are the CLI/output contract. There are no\n48\tdependencies between tasks; the order is by severity of consequence. Tasks 2 and 9 both come from\n49\tfinding #9 and are split by file — Task 2 owns the `binder.pairs` parser change, Task 9 owns the\n50\tdocs — so run Task 2 first if you run them in the same session.\n51\t\n52\t---\n53\t\n54\t### Task 1: Stop curl reading `~/.curlrc` before the credential-bearing config\n55\t\n56\t**Fixes findings:** #1\n57\t\n58\t`argv` is `{\"curl\", \"-K\", \"-\"}`, so curl parses `$CURL_HOME/.curlrc` (else `$HOME/.curlrc`)\n59\t*before* the `-K -` document carrying the resolved secret. A `trace-ascii` or `proxy` directive\n60\tthere captures the plaintext `Authorization` header. Writing one file under `$HOME` is a weaker\n61\tcapability than the env-var read §5a concedes, so this is inside the claimed boundary.\n62\t\n63\t**Files:**\n64\t- `internal/curl/config.go` (modify)\n65\t- `internal/curl/render.go` (modify)\n66\t- `internal/canary/canary_test.go` (modify)\n67\t\n68\t**Steps:**\n69\t1. In `BuildConfigWith` (config.go:103), change `argv` to `{\"curl\", \"-q\", \"-K\", \"-\"}`. Both the\n70\t   early-return argv and the success argv come from this one variable, so the single edit covers\n71\t   the `req == nil` and `doc.build` error paths too. `-q` must be the first parameter — curl\n72\t   ignores it elsewhere.\n73\t2. Add a comment at that line recording *why* `-q` is load-bearing: without it a writable\n74\t   `.curlrc` reads the credential out of the `-K` document.\n75\t3. Mirror the flag in the rendered curl (`internal/curl/render.go`) so the copy-pasteable\n76\t   reproduction behaves the same as the call talaria made.\n77\t4. Add a canary stage in `canary_test.go` that writes a `.curlrc` containing\n78\t   `trace-ascii = <path under the harness temp dir>` into the harness `HOME` (already set at\n79\t   canary_test.go:188), runs a call carrying the canary, and asserts the trace file does not\n80\t   exist — and, if it does, that it does not contain the canary.\n81\t\n82\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/curl/... ./internal/canary/...`\n83\t- [ ] With a `.curlrc` containing `trace-ascii` planted in `HOME`, a call carrying the canary\n84\t      writes no trace file and leaks nothing.\n85\t- [ ] `BuildConfigWith` returns argv beginning `curl -q -K -` on the success path and on both\n86\t      error paths.\n87\t\n88\t---\n89\t"
