        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "88\t\n89\tThe rendered curl now starts `curl -q -s`, so the `curl -s` examples in `README.md`, `AGENT.md`\n90\tand the `call` output sketch in DESIGN.md §\"Output shape\" were updated to match.\n91\t\n92\t---\n93\t\n94\t### Task 2: Never echo a rejected flag's value, and reject malformed header names\n95\t\n96\t**Fixes findings:** #2, #9 (the silent-corruption half)\n97\t\n98\t`b.fail(\"%s %q is not name=value\", flag, raw)` puts the whole rejected argument into the exit-2\n99\tJSON on stderr, so `--header \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"` — the form AGENT.md currently\n100\tdocuments — prints the real token. The `--body` variant joins *every* body value into one\n101\tmessage, and request bodies routinely carry `client_secret`/`password`. Separately,\n102\t`--header 'X-Trace: abc=1'` is *accepted*, cut at the first `=`, and sends the malformed wire\n103\theader `X-Trace: abc: 1`.\n104\t\n105\t**Files:**\n106\t- `internal/request/build.go` (modify)\n107\t- `internal/request/build_test.go` (modify)\n108\t- `internal/canary/canary_test.go` (modify)\n109\t\n110\t**Steps:**\n111\t1. In `binder.pairs` (build.go:311), report the position and the name half only, never the value:\n112\t   `%s %d is not name=value` with the 1-based index, plus the text before the first `=` or `:`\n113\t   when there is one. Elide the value entirely — do not include a truncated prefix of it.\n114\t2. In the same function, reject a name containing `:`, whitespace, or any other character not\n115\t   valid in an HTTP field name, with a message naming the offending *name* only. This closes\n116\t   finding #9's silent corruption: `X-Trace: abc=1` becomes a clean exit 2 instead of a malformed\n117\t   header. Accepting the curl-style `Name: value` form is deliberately **not** done here —\n118\t   DESIGN.md §4 specifies `name=value`, and Task 9 fixes the docs to match.\n119\t3. In the `--body` failure path (the flag declared at build.go:53), report the count and the\n120\t   *kind* of each value (literal / `@file` / `-`), never the bytes.\n121\t4. Update any existing test asserting the old message text.\n122\t5. Add a canary stage: a malformed `--header` and a malformed `--body` each carrying the canary,\n123\t   scanned across stdout, stderr, every `--output` format, the report and the history store.\n124\t\n125\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/request/... ./internal/canary/...`\n126\t- [ ] `--header 'Authorization: Bearer <canary>'` exits 2 with the canary absent from every\n127\t      output surface."
      }
