        "name": "Bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "git add -A internal/request internal/canary tasks.json && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix: never echo a rejected name=value flag's value, reject bad header names\n\nA rejected --header/--query/--param is now reported by position with the\nvalue elided: the shell expands `--header \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"`\nbefore talaria sees it, so quoting the argument back put the real token in\nthe exit-2 message on stderr. The message carries the flag's 1-based index\nand, when the argument holds a `=` or `:`, the text before it -- a name,\nnever a prefix of the value.\n\nA repeated --body now reports the count and the kind of each value\n(literal / @file / stdin) instead of joining the bodies, which routinely\ncarry client_secret or password.\n\n--header names are held to the RFC 9110 token set, so `X-Trace: abc=1` is a\nclean exit 2 rather than the malformed wire header `X-Trace: abc: 1` it\nused to become. --query keeps no such rule: a query parameter name is not\nan HTTP field name.\n\nCovers findings #2 and the silent-corruption half of #9, with a canary\nstage driving the malformed flags through every --output format and the\nhistory store -- verified to fail against the pre-fix binder.\nEOF\n)\"",
          "description": "Commit the fix"
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      }
    ],
