        "type": "text",
        "text": "Task 2 done and committed. Stopping here.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `internal/request/build.go` — `pairs` now reports a rejected argument by 1-based position with the value elided (`--header 1 is not name=value (it starts \"Authorization\"; the rest is not echoed)`), and echoes nothing at all when the argument holds neither `=` nor `:`, since such an argument is indistinguishable from a bare token. `--param` was leaking the same way and got the same treatment. `--header` names are now validated against the RFC 9110 token set via a `nameRule`; `--query` deliberately has no rule, so `filter[status]=open` still binds.\n- `internal/request/body.go` — a repeated `--body` reports `2 times (literal, @file)` instead of joining the bodies.\n- Tests: value-elision table in `request_test.go`, field-name rejection, a query-name-that-a-header-would-reject case, byte-elision for `--body`, and a new `TestAMalformedFlagDoesNotEchoItsValue` canary stage running the malformed flags through every `--output` format plus the history store.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- The new canary stage was run against the pre-fix binder (`git stash` of the two source files): it failed, reporting the canary on both stderr surfaces. It is a real gate, not a vacuous pass.\n- `go test ./...` — all 15 packages green.\n- `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` — clean.\n\nNo doc changes: the `--header Name: value` syntax in AGENT.md is Task 9's scope, which the plan explicitly assigns there."
