        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "125\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/request/... ./internal/canary/...`\n126\t- [ ] `--header 'Authorization: Bearer <canary>'` exits 2 with the canary absent from every\n127\t      output surface.\n128\t- [ ] Repeated `--body` with two secret-bearing values reports two bodies by kind, no bytes.\n129\t- [ ] `--header 'X-Trace: abc=1'` exits 2 rather than sending `X-Trace: abc: 1`.\n130\t\n131\t---\n132\t\n133\t### Task 3: Reject credentials in a base URL's userinfo\n134\t\n135\t**Fixes findings:** #3\n136\t\n137\t`baseURL` validates scheme and host but keeps `parsed.User`, so `http://user:pass@host` from\n138\t`--base-url`, a profile, **or a spec's `servers[0].url` (untrusted input)** reaches `request.url`,\n139\tthe emitted `request.curl` (render.go:146), and `history.jsonl` (entry.go:154) in cleartext — a\n140\tpermanent artifact with no way to get the value back out short of deleting the store.\n141\t\n142\t**Files:**\n143\t- `internal/request/build.go` (modify)\n144\t- `cmd/talaria/history.go` (modify)\n145\t- `internal/request/build_test.go` (modify)\n146\t- `internal/canary/canary_test.go` (modify)\n147\t\n148\t**Steps:**\n149\t1. In `baseURL` (build.go:144), after the scheme/host check, reject `parsed.User != nil` via\n150\t   `b.fail`, naming the source (`--base-url`, the profile, or the spec's `servers[0].url`) and\n151\t   pointing at `TALARIA_AUTH_BASIC` as the supported path. Rejecting rather than stripping is the\n152\t   right call: talaria already has a basic-auth path that keeps the value symbolic, and silently\n153\t   dropping the userinfo would send an unauthenticated request the caller thinks is\n154\t   authenticated. The message must not echo the userinfo — report the host only.\n155\t2. Apply the same check in `replayRequest` (history.go:511), which re-parses a URL read off disk,\n156\t   alongside the existing `IsHTTPScheme` guard and for the reason its comment already states.\n157\t3. Add unit cases for all three sources plus the replay path.\n158\t4. Add a canary stage passing `--base-url http://user:<canary>@host` and scanning every surface.\n159\t\n160\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/request/... ./cmd/talaria/... ./internal/canary/...`\n161\t- [ ] `--base-url 'http://admin:s3cr3t@127.0.0.1:8898'` exits 2, and `s3cr3t` appears in no\n162\t      output and in no freshly-created `history.jsonl`.\n163\t- [ ] A spec whose `servers[0].url` carries userinfo is rejected the same way.\n164\t"
      }
    ]
