  "result": "Task 3 done — stopping here.\n\n**What was built:** `talaria` now refuses a base URL carrying credentials in its userinfo.\n\n- `request.Userinfo(raw)` (`internal/request/request.go`) splits `user:password@` off a URL's authority **textually, before `url.Parse`** — the parse-error path quotes the whole URL, so a check running after it would have had nothing left to protect.\n- `binder.baseURL` (`internal/request/build.go:145`) rejects it from all three sources, naming the host only and pointing at `TALARIA_AUTH_BASIC`. Rejecting rather than stripping: a stripped userinfo sends an unauthenticated request the caller thinks is authenticated.\n- `replayRequest` (`cmd/talaria/history.go:504`) applies the same check ahead of the existing scheme guard, since a stored entry is an editable file.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Full suite green: `go test ./...` — all 15 packages `ok`, including the canary suite (6.2s, not cached).\n- Lint green: `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...`.\n- New tests failed first for the right reason (Build *succeeded* and returned `BaseURL:http://admin:s3cr3t@127.0.0.1:8898`; the unparseable case echoed `s3cr3t` in its message).\n- Plan's manual check, run against the built binary: `--base-url 'http://admin:s3cr3t@127.0.0.1:8898'` exits 2 with `base URL from --base-url carries a credential in its userinfo (user:password@127.0.0.1:8898); ... set TALARIA_AUTH_BASIC=...` — no `admin`, no `s3cr3t`.\n\n**Deviation from the plan worth noting:** step 1 said to place the check *after* the scheme/host check. I put it before, because `ftp://u:p@h` and any unparseable URL would otherwise leak the password through the existing `base URL %q ... is not an absolute http(s) URL` message. A unit test (`TestBuildRejectsCredentialsInAnUnparseableBaseURL`) pins that.\n\nDocs updated in `README.md` and `AGENT.md`; `tasks.json` task 3 marked done and committed as `c2a2486`.",
  "ttft_ms": 2150,
  "ttft_stream_ms": 1602,
