        "content": "160\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/request/... ./cmd/talaria/... ./internal/canary/...`\n161\t- [ ] `--base-url 'http://admin:s3cr3t@127.0.0.1:8898'` exits 2, and `s3cr3t` appears in no\n162\t      output and in no freshly-created `history.jsonl`.\n163\t- [ ] A spec whose `servers[0].url` carries userinfo is rejected the same way.\n164\t\n165\t---\n166\t\n167\t### Task 4: Apply `redact.headers` to the displayed request and the emitted curl\n168\t\n169\t**Fixes findings:** #4\n170\t\n171\t`hide()` hard-codes `var builtin *secret.Redactor` (nil = built-ins only) and `cfg.Redact.Headers`\n172\tonly ever reaches `corpus.Redactors` (call.go:239). The result is inverted against DESIGN.md:339\n173\tand README.md:209: the *history entry* stores `<redacted>` while stdout's `request.headers` and\n174\t`request.curl` print the value in the clear — the permanent artifact is protected and the surface\n175\tthe agent reads is not. No test at any level covers `redact.headers`.\n176\t\n177\t**Files:**\n178\t- `internal/request/build.go` (modify)\n179\t- `cmd/talaria/call.go` (modify)\n180\t- `cmd/talaria/run.go` (modify)\n181\t- `internal/request/build_test.go` (modify)\n182\t- `internal/canary/canary_test.go` (modify)\n183\t\n184\t**Steps:**\n185\t1. Add a `Redactor *secret.Redactor` field to `request.Inputs`, documented as the config file's\n186\t   user-extensible display patterns layered over the non-configurable built-in floor.\n187\t2. Change `hide()` (build.go:289) to take that `*secret.Redactor` and use it in place of the\n188\t   local `var builtin`. A nil value must keep meaning built-ins only, so every existing caller and\n189\t   test is unaffected — `secret.Redactor.IsSensitive` already has a nil receiver path.\n190\t3. Thread it at every `request.Build` call site (`cmd/talaria/call.go`, `cmd/talaria/run.go`, and\n191\t   any other) from `secret.NewRedactor(cfg.Redact.Headers...)`, the same construction\n192\t   `newRedactors` uses at call.go:239.\n193\t4. Confirm the query and cookie paths pick it up too — `hide` is shared by all three at\n194\t   build.go:78-80, which is what README.md:209 promises.\n195\t5. Add a canary stage that configures `redact.headers` with a glob and greps stdout, `--dry-run`\n196\t   and pretty output for the value.\n197\t\n198\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/request/... ./cmd/talaria/... ./internal/canary/...`\n199\t- [ ] With `redact: {headers: [\"x-session-*\"]}`, `X-Session-Id` renders `<redacted>` in\n200\t      `request.headers`, in `request.curl`, in pretty output and in `--dry-run`.\n201\t- [ ] Built-in-only behaviour is unchanged when the config sets no extra patterns."
