        "text": "Task 4 done and committed. Stopping here.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `internal/request/build.go`: added `Inputs.Redactor *secret.Redactor`; `hide()` now takes it instead of hard-coding `var builtin *secret.Redactor`. Nil still means built-ins only, so every prior caller is unaffected.\n- `cmd/talaria/call.go` and `cmd/talaria/run.go`: threaded the config's redactor into both `request.Build` call sites — `run` reuses the `r.redactors.Request` it already built from the same config, so display and history cannot disagree.\n- Coverage: two unit tests in `internal/request/request_test.go` (all three locations — header, query, cookie — plus the nil/built-ins-only case), and a canary stage in `internal/canary/canary_test.go` iterating json/pretty/tsv across `--dry-run`, a real call, and both history commands, with a control test asserting `X-Session-Id` is *not* redacted without config.\n- `README.md`: the `redact.headers` paragraph now states the patterns cover query parameters and cookies too, and lists the surfaces they hide on.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- Red confirmed for the right reason: the three locations printed the canary before the fix.\n- The canary stage was checked against a reverted `call.go` — it fails with 2 leaked surfaces per format, so it's a real regression guard, not a vacuous pass.\n- `go test ./...` fully green; `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` clean.\n\nOne deliberate divergence from the plan: it named `internal/request/build_test.go`, which doesn't exist — the sibling `hide` tests live in `request_test.go`, so the new ones went there. I did not write that note into `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, because inserting lines would shift the `line_start`/`line_end` ranges that tasks 5–9 in `tasks.json` still point at."
