        "content": "195\t5. Add a canary stage that configures `redact.headers` with a glob and greps stdout, `--dry-run`\n196\t   and pretty output for the value.\n197\t\n198\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/request/... ./cmd/talaria/... ./internal/canary/...`\n199\t- [ ] With `redact: {headers: [\"x-session-*\"]}`, `X-Session-Id` renders `<redacted>` in\n200\t      `request.headers`, in `request.curl`, in pretty output and in `--dry-run`.\n201\t- [ ] Built-in-only behaviour is unchanged when the config sets no extra patterns.\n202\t\n203\t---\n204\t\n205\t### Task 5: Redact response bodies that are arrays or contain arrays\n206\t\n207\t**Fixes findings:** #5\n208\t\n209\t`decodeObject` rejects any body not starting with `{`, and `redactPath` only descends into\n210\t`map[string]any`. A top-level JSON array and an array nested under an object — two very common\n211\tshapes — are returned unchanged, so the built-in `access_token`/`refresh_token`/`id_token` paths\n212\tand any configured `redact.body-paths` silently do nothing and, because §5a mandates redaction at\n213\twrite time, the value lands permanently in `history.jsonl`. `TestBodySkipsNonJSONBodies`\n214\tcurrently **asserts the leak as correct behaviour**.\n215\t\n216\t**Files:**\n217\t- `internal/secret/response.go` (modify)\n218\t- `internal/secret/response_test.go` (modify)\n219\t- `internal/canary/canary_test.go` (modify)\n220\t\n221\t**Steps:**\n222\t1. Rename/repurpose `decodeObject` (response.go:155) to decode into `any`, accepting a leading\n223\t   `[` as well as `{`. Keep both existing guards exactly as they are: `dec.UseNumber()` (so a\n224\t   large id is not rewritten through float64) and the trailing-token `io.EOF` check (so a body\n225\t   ending in junk is not re-encoded).\n226\t2. Change `redactPath` (response.go:190) to take `any` and fan out across `[]any` at each\n227\t   segment: applying `items.access_token` to every element of `items`, and a top-level\n228\t   `access_token` to every element of a top-level array. Report `true` if any element matched.\n229\t3. Update the encode side to round-trip a non-object root.\n230\t4. Retarget `TestBodySkipsNonJSONBodies` (response_test.go:127): `[{\"access_token\":\"x\"}]` moves\n231\t   out of the skip list into a new case asserting it *is* redacted; `\"not json at all\"` stays.\n232\t5. Add both array shapes to the canary suite so the store is gated on them.\n233\t\n234\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/secret/... ./internal/canary/...`\n235\t- [ ] `[{\"access_token\":\"TOPSECRET-ARR\"}]` and `{\"items\":[{\"access_token\":\"TOPSECRET-NEST\"}]}`\n236\t      are both redacted on stdout and in `history.jsonl`.\n237\t- [ ] Object bodies, non-JSON bodies and large integer ids behave exactly as before.\n238\t\n239\t---"
      }
    ]
