      {
        "tool_use_id": "toolu_016hdKrspumbH5ddXkwPz5wb",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "237\t- [ ] Object bodies, non-JSON bodies and large integer ids behave exactly as before.\n238\t\n239\t---\n240\t\n241\t### Task 6: Handle signals so a killed talaria does not orphan curl or leak the raw capture\n242\t\n243\t**Fixes findings:** #6\n244\t\n245\tNothing installs a signal handler and all cleanup is `defer`-based, so an unhandled signal runs\n246\tnone of it. Confirmed: curl is reparented to `ppid=1` and the request **completes 8s after talaria\n247\tis dead** (so Ctrl-C on an `--allow-mutations` POST does not cancel the write, and `recordCall`\n248\tnever runs, so the call is absent from history); and the capture directory survives holding the\n249\t*raw, unredacted* response, along with the `talaria-body-*` request-body temp file\n250\t(config.go:291).\n251\t\n252\t**Files:**\n253\t- `cmd/talaria/root.go` (modify)\n254\t- `internal/curl/exec.go` (modify)\n255\t- `internal/curl/exec_test.go` (modify)\n256\t\n257\t**Steps:**\n258\t1. In `cmd/talaria/root.go`, wrap execution in\n259\t   `signal.NotifyContext(context.Background(), os.Interrupt, syscall.SIGTERM)` and thread that\n260\t   context down to `curl.ExecuteWith`.\n261\t2. In `exec.go:77`, derive the timeout context from the passed-in ctx instead of\n262\t   `context.Background()`, so both cancellation sources kill curl through the existing\n263\t   `CommandContext` and every `defer` (capture cleanup, config cleanup) runs normally.\n264\t3. Set `cmd.SysProcAttr = &syscall.SysProcAttr{Setpgid: true}` with a `cmd.Cancel` that signals\n265\t   `-pgid`, so anything curl spawned dies with it. This is unix-only — put it behind the same\n266\t   build-tag split `internal/corpus` already uses for `lock`, with a no-op elsewhere, so the\n267\t   non-unix build keeps compiling.\n268\t4. For SIGKILL, which no handler can catch: sweep stale `talaria-call-*` and `talaria-body-*`\n269\t   directories under `TMPDIR` at start-up, removing only those older than a conservative age and\n270\t   only ones talaria itself named.\n271\t5. Test that a cancelled context terminates curl and removes both the capture directory and the\n272\t   `talaria-body-*` temp file.\n273\t\n274\t**Verify:** `go test ./internal/curl/... ./cmd/talaria/...`\n275\t- [ ] Cancelling the context mid-call kills curl rather than orphaning it, and leaves no\n276\t      `talaria-call-*` or `talaria-body-*` behind."
      }
    ]
  },
  "parent_tool_use_id": null,
  "session_id": "1722d72a-0d22-4133-b403-064225f75806",
  "uuid": "5469149c-0366-442d-ab72-5a9f06089aaa",
