        "content": "277\t- [x] The un-signalled path is unchanged: `go test -race ./...` stays green.\n278\t\n279\t---\n280\t\n281\t### Task 7: Give history entries a stable id so `replay` cannot re-issue the wrong request\n282\t\n283\t**Fixes findings:** #7\n284\t\n285\tThe index is `len(entries) - position` (history.go:271), recomputed on every read, and\n286\t`corpus.Entry` carries no stable identifier. `call`, `run` **and `replay` itself** all append, so\n287\tevery index in a previously-printed listing silently shifts. Confirmed: `history replay 2` then\n288\t`history replay 1` replayed the *same* entry twice. Two replays in a row is ordinary agent\n289\tbehaviour, and the e2e suite cannot catch it because it replays index 1 exactly once.\n290\t\n291\t**Files:**\n292\t- `internal/corpus/entry.go` (modify)\n293\t- `internal/corpus/store.go` (modify)\n294\t- `cmd/talaria/history.go` (modify)\n295\t- `internal/corpus/store_test.go` (modify)\n296\t- `AGENT.md` (modify)\n297\t\n298\t**Steps:**\n299\t1. Add a stable `ID string` to `corpus.Entry`, assigned at append time. Use the entry's\n300\t   RFC3339Nano timestamp: it needs no counter state in the file, is already monotonic per process,\n301\t   and survives the trim path — but make `Append` disambiguate a collision (two entries in the\n302\t   same nanosecond) rather than emit a duplicate id.\n303\t2. Tolerate entries already on disk with no id: an old store must keep listing and showing, so an\n304\t   empty id renders as such rather than erroring the whole read.\n305\t3. Have `history` list print the id alongside the positional index, in the JSON view and as a\n306\t   column in the table/TSV rows.\n307\t4. Have `show` and `replay` accept either: an id when the argument matches one, the positional\n308\t   index otherwise. Keep the positional form working — it is documented — but resolve the id\n309\t   first so an unambiguous id always wins.\n310\t5. Document the id as the stable handle in `AGENT.md`'s history section, and say plainly that\n311\t   positional indices shift on every write.\n312\t6. Test the exact confirmed sequence: list, replay one entry, then replay a *different* id and\n313\t   assert it replayed that one.\n314\t"
      }
    ]
