        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "215\t| 2 | Usage error: unknown command or operation, missing parameter, bad flag, or a mutation without `--allow-mutations` | fix the invocation using `valid_alternatives` and the message |\n216\t| 3 | The spec could not be read or parsed | check the path or URL; do not retry unchanged |\n217\t| 4 | With `--fail-on-error`: the response was an HTTP error or violated the spec | read the `validation` block and `response.status` on stdout; report what failed |\n218\t| 5 | A required credential is not set | tell a human which variable to export; do not retry until they have |\n219\t\n220\t## History\n221\t\n222\tEvery real call is recorded, redacted at write time, newest first. Use it instead of re-issuing a\n223\trequest to remember what happened:\n224\t\n225\t```sh\n226\ttalaria history --operation getPet --status 4xx\n227\ttalaria history show 3\n228\t```\n229\t\n230\tThe index `history` prints is the entry's position in the whole store, so it stays valid under\n231\tfilters. `talaria history replay <n>` re-sends an entry and records the result as a new one;\n232\treplaying a mutation needs `--allow-mutations` too. Dry runs are never recorded. Recording is off\n233\twhere a profile says so, or everywhere under `TALARIA_HISTORY=off` — if history is empty, that is\n234\tusually why.\n235\t\n236\tCredentials are stored as names, so nothing in history can be read back into a value.\n237\t\n238\t## Rules\n239\t\n240\t1. Never ask a human for a credential value. Ask them to export a named variable.\n241\t2. Never add `--allow-mutations` silently.\n242\t3. Treat a 4xx as data, not as a crash. Exit 0 means talaria worked.\n243\t4. Prefer `describe` over reading the spec, and `history` over repeating a call.\n244\t5. Use `--dry-run` when you are unsure what a request will look like. It costs nothing."
