          "command": "git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix: give history entries a stable id so replay names one entry\n\nThe index was len(entries) - position, recomputed on every read, and every\ncommand that reads history also appends to it — replay included. So a listing's\nindices are stale the moment anything records, and `replay 2; replay 1` re-issues\nthe same entry twice.\n\nStore.Append now assigns each entry an id under the append lock: its RFC3339Nano\ntimestamp, with a counting suffix when the instant is already taken. `history`\nprints it in the JSON view and as a column, and `show` and `replay` resolve an id\nfirst and fall back to the documented positional index. Entries written before\nids existed keep listing, with an empty id rather than an invented one.\nEOF\n)\"",
          "description": "Commit the change"
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      }
    ],
