        "text": "Task 7 complete and committed.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `internal/corpus/entry.go` — `Entry.ID` (`json:\"id,omitempty\"`), the stable handle.\n- `internal/corpus/store.go` — `Append` assigns the id inside the existing lock/write/trim critical section, using the entry's RFC3339Nano timestamp with a `#n` suffix when that instant is already taken. `lineSource` became `lineHead`, which reads both the source (retention cap) and the id (collision check) off a raw line.\n- `cmd/talaria/history.go` — list carries `id` in the JSON view and as an `ID` column (`-` for pre-id entries); `selectEntry` resolves an id first, then the 1-based positional index, with a usage error naming both forms.\n- `AGENT.md` / `README.md` — the id is documented as the stable handle, with the reason indices shift on every write stated plainly.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- Red confirmed for the right reason: with the source stashed and only the field present, `history show <id>` failed with `history index \"\" is not a number`, and the list showed no ids.\n- Green: `go test ./...` and `go test -race ./...` both fully pass; `go build ./...`, `gofmt -l .` and `go vet ./...` clean.\n- The confirmed sequence from the finding is now a test — two calls, list, replay one id, replay the other, assert the server saw the second entry's path — plus store-level tests for id stability, same-nanosecond disambiguation, and old id-less stores still reading.\n\n`tasks.json` task 7 is marked `done: true`. Tasks 8 and 9 remain. Stopping here."
