        "content": "346\t**Built as:** step 1's `RunE: cmd.Help()` would have kept bare `talaria auth` at exit 0, which the\n347\ttitle and the check below both reject, so `groupCommand`'s `RunE` returns\n348\t`clierr.Usage(\"%q requires a subcommand\")` carrying the subcommand names in `valid_alternatives`.\n349\tNo help block is printed on either path: stderr carries one JSON object, and prose in front of it\n350\tis what `SilenceUsage` was set to avoid. `history` was checked per step 2 and left alone — it is\n351\trunnable (it lists), not a parent-only group, and `usageArgs(cobra.NoArgs)` already exits 2 there.\n352\t\n353\t**Verify:** `go test ./cmd/talaria/...`\n354\t- [x] `talaria auth` and `talaria auth chekc` both exit 2 with a structured error on stderr.\n355\t- [ ] `talaria auth check <spec>` is unaffected.\n356\t\n357\t---\n358\t\n359\t### Task 9: Correct the documented `--header` syntax and gate the docs on it\n360\t\n361\t**Fixes findings:** #9 (documentation half; the parser change is Task 2)\n362\t\n363\tDESIGN.md §4 specifies `--header X-Foo=bar` and the code implements it, but AGENT.md's headline\n364\t`call` example is `--header 'X-Trace: abc'`, which exits 2 — and per finding #2 the resulting\n365\terror echoes whatever secret the agent put there. §3.7 makes AGENT.md a first-class deliverable\n366\tand this is the one line an LLM copies verbatim. `agentdoc_test.go` checks command names, exit\n367\tcodes and env vars but never flag argument syntax, so this drifted unpoliced.\n368\t\n369\t**Files:**\n370\t- `AGENT.md` (modify)\n371\t- `README.md` (modify)\n372\t- `cmd/talaria/agentdoc_test.go` (modify)\n373\t\n374\t**Steps:**\n375\t1. Fix `AGENT.md:54` (`--header 'X-Trace: abc'` → `--header X-Trace=abc`) and `AGENT.md:169`\n376\t   (`--header 'X-Api-Key: sk-live-…'` → `--header X-Api-Key=sk-live-…`).\n377\t2. Fix `README.md:274` (`--header \"X-Api-Key: sk-live-…\"`) the same way. README.md:251, :259 and\n378\t   :421 mention `--header` without an argument and need no change — confirm before editing.\n379\t3. Extend `agentdoc_test.go` to extract the fenced `talaria …` invocations from AGENT.md and\n380\t   execute each against a fixture spec with `--dry-run`, asserting a non-usage exit. This is the\n381\t   part that stops the next drift; without it the doc fix is a one-off.\n382\t4. Skip or annotate any fenced invocation that legitimately cannot run under `--dry-run`, with the\n383\t   reason stated inline rather than by silently narrowing the extraction.\n384\t\n385\t**Verify:** `go test ./cmd/talaria/...`\n386\t- [ ] Every `talaria …` invocation in AGENT.md runs against the fixture spec without a usage\n387\t      error.\n388\t- [ ] No `--header 'Name: value'` form remains in AGENT.md or README.md.\n389\t"
