        "content": "93:      id*: (string) Unique identifier\n189:from every source, including a stored history entry on the way to a replay. A base URL is copied\n366:talaria history replay 3\n369:`history` lists the store newest first: index, id, time, source, method, path, status, operation.\n372:or `replay` — so a smoke run over a large spec does not bury the calls you made by hand. The\n373:index is an entry's position in the whole store, not in the filtered list, so a filter does not\n374:renumber it — but a *write* does, and `call`, `run` and `replay` all write. The id is the handle\n375:that does not move: it is assigned once, at record time, and both `show` and `replay` prefer it\n376:over an index. Entries written before ids existed have none and list as `-`.\n378:`history show <id|n>` prints one entry in full; `history replay <id|n>` sends it again and records\n381:in the file to read back. It is gated the same way `call` is: replaying a `POST` needs\n383:reproduced, and replay says so on stderr rather than pretending it sent one.\n392:and a replay would send something the original call did not; `history show` reports such a body",
