        "text": "Task 9 done — the last one in `tasks.json`.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `AGENT.md:54` and `:174`, `README.md:288` — `--header 'X-Trace: abc'` → `--header X-Trace=abc`. This was curl's syntax, not talaria's; the documented line exits 2, and per finding #2 the error used to echo the header value. README's other three `--header` mentions carry no argument and were left alone, as the plan asked me to confirm.\n- `cmd/talaria/agentdoc_test.go` — two new tests, since the doc fix alone would have been a one-off:\n  - `TestAgentDocInvocationsAreAcceptedAsWritten` extracts every fenced `talaria …` line, splits it shell-style (quotes and trailing `#` comments), substitutes `testdata/call.yaml` for `./openapi.yaml`, appends `--dry-run` to commands that register it, and requires a non-usage exit. Two invocations can't run — `run` has no `--dry-run` and points at a dead host, `history show <id>` names an entry an isolated history lacks — so both sit in a `notRunnable` map keyed by the doc's own line, annotated rather than extracted around (plan step 4).\n  - `TestDocsWriteHeadersAsNameEqualsValue` covers the prose outside the fences in both docs.\n\n**Verification** — red first: the new test failed on exactly the `--header 'X-Trace: abc'` line with `--header 1 is not name=value`. After the fix, `go test ./...` is green across all 15 packages, and `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` passes. I also confirmed the header-form guard is non-vacuous by temporarily reintroducing the old syntax and watching it fail.\n\nSince this closed the last task, I did the final conventions pass and found two README gaps against shipped behaviour: the exit-code table omitted the group-without-subcommand case task 8 added, and the AGENT.md section described the doc tests as they were before they executed examples. Both fixed in a separate commit."
      }
