    "content": [
      {
        "type": "tool_use",
        "id": "toolu_01169B27FvFuehrb6E82u6Uu",
        "name": "Agent",
        "input": {
          "description": "Security review of branch",
          "subagent_type": "general-purpose",
          "run_in_background": true,
          "prompt": "You are the SECURITY reviewer for the Go CLI project `talaria` at /home/casper/projects/talaria (branch `ralph/design`, base `main`).\n\n`main` contains only docs — the ENTIRE Go codebase on this branch is the diff. Get the changed-file list with `git diff --name-only main...HEAD`. Read the actual source files (the diff is 29k lines; reading files directly is better than dumping the diff).\n\nCRITICAL CONTEXT: The product IS a credential firewall. Read `docs/design/DESIGN.md` §5a (\"The credential firewall\") in full — it is the security spec. Invariant: **no consumer of stdout or stderr ever observes a credential value**, and no credential value may reach history/corpus files, emitted curl, dry-run output, error messages, JUnit reports, or debug logs. Secrets must never be argv elements (curl is fed a config document on its stdin via `curl -K -`).\n\nKey files to audit: internal/secret/{secret,redact,response}.go, internal/curl/{config,exec,render,version,sweep}.go, internal/request/{build,body,request}.go, internal/corpus/{entry,store}.go, internal/config/{auth,config}.go, internal/canary/surfaces.go, cmd/talaria/*.go, internal/spec/source.go.\n\nYour checklist:\n- Injection: is user/spec input parameterized in shell calls and file paths? curl argv construction, glob handling, `--` separators, header/URL injection via CRLF or newline into the curl config document (this is a config-file format — can a header value or body break out of it and inject new curl directives like `output=` or `upload-file=`?).\n- Secret leakage on EVERY surface: json, pretty, tsv, dry-run, stderr errors, junit, history file, corpus, curl stderr passthrough, panics.\n- Path traversal: spec paths, --fixtures dir, --corpus, temp files for bodies (mode 0600? deleted after exec? races?).\n- File permissions: config file 0600 enforcement, history/corpus file modes.\n- SSRF / remote spec fetch: internal/spec/source.go fetches URLs and caches them — scheme restrictions, redirect handling, cache poisoning, $ref resolution to remote or local files.\n- Secrets committed in the diff.\n- Symlink handling on spec/cache/corpus paths.\n\nA PRIOR review already found and FIXED these 9 (verify the fixes are actually correct and complete — an incomplete fix is a new CRIT):\n1. curl reads ~/.curlrc → fixed with `-q`\n2. malformed --header/--body echoed the value into the error → fixed\n3. credentials in base URL userinfo → rejected\n4. redact.headers config not applied to displayed request/emitted curl → fixed\n5. response-body redaction failed on array-shaped bodies → fixed\n6. signal handling: orphaned curl + leaked raw capture → fixed\n7. history positional indices → stable ids\n8. `talaria auth` with no subcommand exited 0 → exits 2\n9. AGENT.md/README documented `--header 'Name: value'` but binary takes `name=value` → docs fixed\n\nThese were reported previously as WARN/INFO and are KNOWN — do NOT re-report them unless you find they are actually CRIT-severity: missing `--globoff`; request bodies only redact 3 RFC6749 fields; built-in sensitive-name list misses `Authentication`; scrubber misses name-matched literals; scrubber corrupts short credentials; curl --version preflight has no timeout; no fsync before rename in corpus replace; CI has no race detector; curl inherits full env.\n\nFocus on NEW issues and on incorrect/incomplete fixes.\n\nReport findings as a numbered list. For each: Title, Severity (CRIT/WARN/INFO), File:line, Description (what is wrong and why it matters), Suggested fix (concrete). Every finding MUST have a real file:line you verified. Verify claims by reading the code — do not speculate. Where you can, prove it with a quick test (`go test`, or a small scratch program in /tmp). Be honest about severity: CRIT = real exploitable leak/bug; WARN = missing hardening; INFO = style/docs."
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      }
