        "content": "<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (261.1KB). Full output saved to: /home/casper/.claude/projects/-home-casper-projects-talaria/1a9982fa-d22f-44f2-b01c-371148e12530/tool-results/bsgv2xcmi.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n.ralph/ralph-20260802-195025.log:2773\n.ralph/ralph-20260802-154350.log:898\n---\n[19:50:25] PHASE 3/5 — BUILD\n[19:53:41] PHASE 4/5 — REVIEW\n[22:34:51] PHASE 5/5 — PULL REQUEST\n--- generic ---\n    \"stdout\": \"commit d1eecd0a082285c9fe5d948a4b304f82f974df6c\\nAuthor: Teeeep <casperjantepe@gmail.com>\\nDate:   Sun Aug 2 15:40:01 2026 +0000\\n\\n    docs: reposition as talaria — Postman for agents\\n    \\n    Positioning: an API client you can hand to an agent. The credential\\n    firewall moves from a design principle to the product's reason to exist.\\n    Postman, Insomnia, Bruno, Hurl and Apidog enter the landscape as the\\n    actual incumbents under this framing; Bruno (44k stars, May 2026) is the\\n    one to beat on developer sentiment, and none of them are trying to solve\\n    the credential problem.\\n    \\n    Adds history, which unifies 'what did I call' with the twin's corpus and\\n    gives the useful half of request chaining via replay. Adds exit code 5\\n    for missing credentials so agents can act on it. Documents the threats\\n    the firewall does not cover.\\n    \\n    Name resolved to talaria — Hermes's winged sandals. The tool is not the\\n    messenger; the agent is.\\n---PREV FINDINGS---\\n## Finding 1: curl reads `~/.curlrc` on every call — one writable file exfiltrates every resolved credential\\n- **Severity:** CRIT\\n- **File:** internal/curl/config.go:103\\n## Finding 2: A malformed `--header`/`--body` flag echoes the credential verbatim into the structured error\\n- **Severity:** CRIT\\n- **File:** internal/request/build.go:311\\n## Finding 3: Credentials in a URL's userinfo reach stdout, the emitted curl, and the permanent history file in cleartext\\n- **Severity:** CRIT\\n- **File:** internal/request/build.go:144\\n## Finding 4: `redact.headers` from the config file never reaches the displayed request or the emitted curl\\n- **Severity:** CRIT\\n- **File:** internal/request/build.go:80\\n## Finding 5: Built-in response-body redaction silently fails on array-shaped bod\n...\n</persisted-output>",
